# `transfer(target=checking, source=savings, note="weekly")` writes its arguments by name, in another order than the
# signature has them: `target` holds the checking account and `source` the savings, though both are Accounts and the
# checking account is written first (#157). `log(target)` is handed the checking account. `note` is filled by a literal
# and holds no value.

route accounts.run
step run/transfer
step run/transfer/log

line entry > run call
line Account·savings > run value
line Account·checking > run value
line Account·savings > run/transfer value                  # `print(source.name, ..)`
line Account·checking > run/transfer/log value             # `log(target)`
line run/transfer > Screen own
line run/transfer/log > Screen own

home Account·savings run
home Account·checking run

side entry left
side Screen right
